ations reference","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/source-to-pay-operations/supplier-lifecycle-operations/supp-mgmt-reference.md","line":33},{"title":"Supplier","target":"supplier","line":38},{"title":"Domain separation for service providers","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-security/domain-sep-landing-page.md","line":62},{"title":"Supplier Lifecycle Operations","target":"supp-mgmt-landing-page","line":66},{"title":"Supplier","target":"supplier","line":67}],"metadata":{"title":"Domain separation and Supplier Lifecycle Operations","description":"If any conrefs are broken, re-add them from the doc/source/reuse/domain-separation/domain-separation-overview.dita file. In the short description, edit the first sentence to state whether domain separation is supported or not and add the application name. Keep the conref at the end that describes domain separation.Domain separation is unsupported for Supplier Lifecycle Operations . Domain separation enables you to separate data, processes, and administrative tasks into logical groupings called domains. You can control several aspects of this separation, including which users can see and access data.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/source-to-pay-operations/supplier-lifecycle-operations/supplier-domain-separation.html","release":"australia","product":"Supplier Lifecycle Operations","classification":"supplier-lifecycle-operations","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":2,"breadcrumb":["Reference","Supplier Lifecycle Operations","Finance and Supply Chain"],"tags":["#source-to-pay-operations","#suppliers","#onboarding","#risk","#s2p","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/source-to-pay-operations/supplier-lifecycle-operations/supplier-domain-separation.md"},
